 "final_summary": "The bug was caused by the boolean parsing function not handling case-insensitive inputs. The fix modifies `parse_bool` in `convert.py` to convert both input text and predefined values to lowercase, enabling correct parsing of mixed-case boolean strings like 'Yes' or 'No'. This ensures the query parameter 'overdue' is properly interpreted regardless of case.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/convert.py b/tracker/convert.py\nindex db3b63f..61d8996 100644\n--- a/tracker/convert.py\n+++ b/tracker/convert.py\n@@ -30,10 +30,11 @@ def parse_bool(value, default=None, name=\"value\"):\n     if isinstance(value, bool):\n         return value\n     text = str(value).strip()\n-    if text in TRUE_VALUES:\n+    if text.lower() in [v.lower() for v in TRUE_VALUES]:\n         return True\n-    if text in FALSE_VALUES:\n+    if text.lower() in [v.lower() for v in FALSE_VALUES]:\n         return False\n+    raise ValidationError(f\"{name} must be a boolean\", {{name: \"not_a_boolean\"}})\n     raise ValidationError(f\"{name} must be a boolean\", {name: \"not_a_boolean\"})\n \n \n",
